<title>FRANCE: French budget - Balance sheet details.</title>
<headline>French budget - Balance sheet details.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government provided the following balance sheet for its 1997 central government budget (figures in millions of francs unless stated).</p>
<p>						 1996	1997    Change</p>
<p> SPENDING							     (pct)</p>
<p>  A) Public debt and guarantees    230,162    235,855    2.47</p>
<p>     - of which public debt	  226,369    232,604    2.75</p>
<p>  B) Civil Budget		    1,069,703  1,074,411    0.44</p>
<p>  C) Military Budget		   241,448    243,338    0.78</p>
<p>  D) Special Treasury Accounts	10,655	 -699     N/A</p>
<p>  E) Total Spending (A+B+C+D)    1,551,969  1,552,905    0.06</p>
<p>REVENUE</p>
<p>  G) Total Net Receipts	    1,264,162  1,269,237     N/A</p>
<p>BALANCE</p>
<p>  H) Central gvt budget deficit   -287,807   -283,668</p>
<p>     As percentage of GDP		  4.0	  3.0</p>
<p>NOTE - France's government debt is expected to rise to 3,799 billion francs in 1997 from 3,538 billion in 1996, documents released with the 1997 budget show.</p>
<p>Total debt was 3,251 billion francs in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
